{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his clever and witty dialogue.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard university, who is dumped by his girlfriend erica albright (played by rooney mara). this event sets off a chain reaction that leads to zuckerberg creating a website called \"facemash,\" which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and attention from the university administration.\n\nzuckerberg is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are members of the rowing team and are also students at harvard. they propose an idea for a social networking site that would allow harvard students to connect with each other. zuckerberg agrees to help them, but soon becomes more interested in creating his own version of the site, which he launches with the help of his friend eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield).\n\nas facebook grows in popularity, zuckerberg and saverin become embroiled in a lawsuit with the winklevoss twins, who claim that zuckerberg stole their idea. the film also explores the complicated relationships between zuckerberg, saverin, and sean parker (played by justin timberlake), a co-founder of napster who becomes involved with facebook.\n\nthe film features excellent performances from the entire cast, with eisenberg standing out as the awkward and introverted zuckerberg. the supporting cast is also impressive, with garfield and hammer delivering standout performances.\n\nthe film's cinematography is also noteworthy, with fincher using a muted color palette to capture the atmosphere of harvard university and the early days of facebook. the score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also excellent, adding to the film's tense and suspenseful atmosphere.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that explores the complexities of friendship, ambition, and the consequences of success. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and the people behind it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11627468466758728}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.6927862816373818e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.03940728306770325}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.3828373084834311e-05}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.24996495246887207}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.05464606732130051}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.18567566573619843}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -7.152560215217818e-07}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -9.298368240706623e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.218656047465629e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04119579493999481}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.017032857984304428}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529859336093068}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00015200339839793742}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0788910835981369}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00016094549209810793}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.08091060072183609}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.11775506287813187}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0017488384619355202}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0036843856796622276}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.00590532785281539}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.06923678517341614}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -0.0008205560734495521}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04554614797234535}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.1343660056591034}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -1.1920930376163597e-07}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -